From 99714c7278d565146ef6612a9cd54ab2feacb1dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taekim <taekim@day34.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 02:55:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Export full page geometry so a reader can place a
 document on its own paper

A reader reproducing a page needs the paper it was authored on, not just the
column of text: page height, all four margins, and the header/footer parts that
sit in those margins. The body area is computed once and its margins derived
from it rather than re-read from PageDef, because the declared values ignore
the binding gutter, odd/even swapping and the oversized-margin fallback, so a
consumer adding them back would not reproduce where the body actually stands.

Master pages (SectionDef.master_pages) are a separate mechanism and stay
unimplemented, noted at the call site.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
